  - A: Implemented a separate scorepeek-catalog core crate whose generation surface is feature-gated, and a scorepeek-catalog-publisher crate that exclusively owns live acquisition, adapters, zero-build federation, packaging, and publisher verification; the distributed scorepeek dependency graph does not enable generation. Added the single Pages workflow with daily/manual/site-only behavior, strict current/frozen artifact carry-forward, no-op preservation, and scheduled failure issue management. Added the exact three-entry ZIP manifest contract, semantic and artifact revision selection, notices, full publisher validation, bounded client verification and storage, URL precedence and policy, conditional GET, atomic activation, 24-hour background update semantics, URL-change fail-closed behavior, and structured diagnostics. Replaced the old host systemd sync path and updated living docs. Added synthetic artifact/update/store regression tests including CRC, digest, redirects, 304 races, lock recovery, active-catalog preservation, and atomicity. Addressed two independent review rounds covering redirect trust, URL leakage, state races, update lock startup blocking, stale validators, crash recovery, and terminal diagnostics; final review found no important issue. Passed targeted catalog and publisher tests, normal scorepeek check, mise run check, full workspace Clippy, the complete mise run test suite, a live three-source zero-build plus fresh-directory verification, and the required post-commit mise run build. The initial Git commit and post-commit build writes were sandbox-denied at .git/index.lock and mise task-source state; both were rerun through approved target-equivalent prefixes. Created local commit 7be79d82 and left the tree clean and one commit ahead of origin/main without push or deployment.
